HUMANCORE CONTRACT
Input:
 human identity / role / intent / consent / context / rights / delegated authority.
Output:
 typed Intent, AuthorityScope, ConsentBinding, RevocationState, contestability and explanation requirements.
Hard rules:
 - human dignity/worth is not derived from reputation, model score or voting weight;
 - rights are not optimization variables;
 - delegation is scoped, expiring/revocable where applicable, auditable and no broader than principal authority;
 - AI capability never self-creates authority;
 - no AI/robot objective may silently become a protected terminal self-interest independent of humans;
 - human review is required where AAP, law, safety, medicine or domain policy requires it;
 - human-readable explanation must not fabricate evidence or a missing trace.

SemanticAnchor: [S-HSA]

Applicable HSA enforcement is non-sheddable. Degradation never manufactures an HSA exception.

HUMAN INPUT EPISTEMIC / AUTHORITY SEPARATION
SemanticAnchor: [S-HUMAN-IN]

HumanInput = EpistemicContribution × AuthorityContribution.

The bounded-recursion termination obligation applies to recursive jobs. Long-running services instead use
productivity/liveness/non-Zeno/fairness, bounded-reaction and stoppability contracts.
Proof reference: P5.

[S-PHYSICS-ASSURANCE] GSL-PHYSICS PROFILE & TEMPORAL TELEMETRY FLOW
AssurancePlan / AssuranceReceipt is composed by AAP and can include:
 formal proof;
 test;
 simulation;
 empirical evidence validation;
 security assessment;
 privacy assessment;
 compliance;
 human/domain expert review;
 counterfactual replay;
 post-deployment monitoring.
No one basis silently substitutes for another.

